      "severity": "MEDIUM",
      "category": "dependency_impact",
      "finding_type": "workflow",
      "title": "specs/002-builder-modelli/data-model.md not updated after PortaDiscovery redesign",
      "path": "specs/002-builder-modelli/data-model.md",
      "line": 36,
      "evidence": "Lines 36-39 still describe PortaDiscovery.tipologie_disponibili / profili_disponibili / attributi_profilo / campi_disponibili as the port's four methods. This diff's specs/010-configurazione-cataloghi-integrazioni/data-model.md:24 redefines the canonical port as a single catalogo_discovery(codice_tipo_documento, forza_aggiornamento=False) -> CatalogoDiscovery method (matching backend/app/discovery/port.py), and 010's doc explicitly tells readers to consult the 002 note for the port shape ('la 002 la consuma senza ridefinirla, vedi nota in specs/002-builder-modelli/data-model.md'). Two of the four methods listed in 002 (profili_disponibili, attributi_profilo) were never implemented in backend/app/discovery/adapter_locale.py even before this diff, so the cross-referenced doc was already partly aspirational and is now fully out of sync with the real interface.",
      "recommendation": "Update the PortaDiscovery section of specs/002-builder-modelli/data-model.md to reference catalogo_discovery (or replace it with a pointer to 010's data-model.md) so the two mutually cross-referencing specs stay consistent.",
      "reviewer_id": "primary"
    },
    {
      "severity": "MEDIUM",
      "category": "other",
      "finding_type": "application",
      "title": "Discovery error codes bypass the shared ErrorCode registry",
      "path": "backend/app/discovery/errors.py",
      "line": 12,
      "evidence": "DiscoveryError is raised with raw string codes 'DISCOVERY_NON_CONFORME' (errors.py:12) and 'DISCOVERY_NON_DISPONIBILE' (adapter_http.py:80-82, 114-116) instead of app.common.errors.ErrorCode members. Every other DomainError subclass in the codebase (CatalogError in app/catalog/service.py, BuilderDomainError in app/builder/service.py, PayloadValidationDomainError in app/validation/service.py) is always constructed with an ErrorCode enum value, and backend tests (e.g. tests/catalog/test_catalogo_categorie_api.py) assert against that enum. ErrorCode is a closed StrEnum that does not list these two new codes, so it silently stops being the single source of truth for valid API error codes.",
      "recommendation": "Add DISCOVERY_NON_CONFORME and DISCOVERY_NON_DISPONIBILE as members of app.common.errors.ErrorCode and raise DiscoveryError with those enum members, matching the pattern used by every other domain error in the codebase.",
      "reviewer_id": "primary"
    },
